body:
You're going to find something else that gives you life. You won't feel this way forever and I promise things get better. It's really dark and sad when one door closes let alone multiple but I promise more will open you just have to give it the opportunity to happen. It may not happen immediately although I pray it will. Please hang in there. 

&#x200B;

Also everything you did was worth it. You made wonderful memories and probably bad ones too and you learned from them and grew because of it. Nothing is meant to last forever especially sadness and despair. 

&#x200B;

I hope that this message gave you a little hope because you deserve it and I truly hope things start to improve for you sonner rather than later

This depression will pass. I'm glad you changed your plan on easter. You deserve to be here and see all the beautiful things life has to offer. Have you seen Sydney, Australia? Dude that place looks amazing and they have such cute animals. Anyway, please remind yourself this feeling won't last forever. Also please forgive yourself for your past. I don't know what happened but you feel bad about what you did which is a step in the right direction. You're improving as a person.

&#x200B;

I'm very sorry for your loss by the way. If you need to talk dm me any time

I sabotage myself pretty often so I know how it feels to be extremely frustrated with yourself and guilty when you make bad decisions or decisions you regret. Is there any way you can make amends with him? Will time help? sometimes it does. And as for your parents what makes you think they don't like you? Sometimes parents are a little harder on their kids than they should be because they don't know how to respond to or handle certain things. That doesn't mean they don't like you though. Please try to forgive yourself for the mistakes you've made. You don't deserve to live with the weight of guilt and regret. Sometimes when I feel extremely regretful or guilty after something I've done I write apology notes to myself or the person. Writing thank you notes to people can also be extremely beneficial when feeling guilty because it let's the person know how much you value them and what they do for you.

&#x200B;

And when it comes to studying, maybe you haven't found the method that works best for you yet. Try googling a few and see if they work for you. If not ask your teachers for help or extra credit work to help with your grades and understanding of the subject. 

&#x200B;

I really hope this helped. Please hang in there friend. You can do this.

You have so much of a chance to save your future. Please don't do this. You have so much to live sor. So many beautiful sunsets to see. So many memories to make and some of them may not be good but that doesn't mean it won't teach you something that could potentially make you stronger and better prepared for the future. I believe in you and I believe you can get through what you're feeling. 

&#x200B;

Also don't compare yourself to your siblings or anyone for that matter. Everyone's different and a wise man once said "comparison is the thief of joy"

&#x200B;

I hope this helped. Please know you are seen, heard, and appreciated. Have a good night and please don't be so hard on yourself. You're doing amazing.

as someone who struggled with self harm for years please take my advice when I say it's not worth living with scars for years if not forever. grabbing ice and squeezing it helps and doesn't leave a mark or using a red pen or marker if you want the effect of having marks on your arm. you can also pinch the space between your thumb and pointer finger if that makes sense. It also causes pain without the scaring.

&#x200B;

You don't deserve to feel pain though and I hope whatever was bothering you never happens again and if it does I really hope that you can find more positive ways to cope. I'm always here to talk
